-- **Config lookup.** Reviewer config is resolved from the project-context doc's metadata at `projects/<slug>/<slug>-project-context.md` (slug from `task.metadata.project`; fallback: lexicographically-smallest `project-context`-tagged doc under `projects/<slug>/`). Keys: `develop_reviewers` (pool of `{name, tool, block_threshold?, system_prompt?, fallback_chain?, model?, effort?}`), `develop_default_reviewers` (names that run when the task doesn't override), `develop_coder` (`{tool?, model?, effort?}`), `develop_fallback_chain`, `develop_max_rounds`, `develop_max_cost_usd`, `develop_image` (the sandbox container image for **every** agent + the test gate, e.g. `"ghcr.io/acme/dev:2026-06"`; default `ralph-sandbox:latest`), `develop_test_command` (test-gate command, **trusted as-is** — no auto-detection or tool-probe), `develop_check_commands` (a `{check = command}` table letting the repo declare its OWN command for a **non-test** gate check — `lint` / `typecheck` / `sast` / `dep-audit` / `coverage` / `semgrep` — run **verbatim** (no `uv`-wrap, no tool-probe, like `develop_test_command`) instead of the catalog canonical; the fix for a canonical command that over-scopes vs the repo's real policy, e.g. `{ typecheck = "make typecheck" }` where a bare `uv run pyright` would scan a test tree full of pre-existing type debt — #273; a task table merges per-key on top; `test` / `format` keys and unknown checks are rejected loudly), `develop_test_gate` (bool; `false` excludes the **`test` check only** from the per-round check-set — it is a *test* escape hatch, not a whole-gate kill switch, so the deterministic `lint` floor still runs — #131/#132/ADR 0003 §10; **generalized by `develop_check_states` — `test_gate=false` ≡ `{ test = "off" }`**), `develop_check_states` (a `{check = state}` table setting a **non-format** gate check's blocking role — `required` / `informational` / `off` — #273 slice 2; `off` **drops** the check cleanly, distinct from a required-but-tool-absent check t